All source books, papers, standards, certificates, data, and software stay at their authorized external locations. Readers can use the publisher’s download choices for a retained copy. The original explanations, worked teaching examples, and learning connections are the content authored here.

Official publisher pages, edition identities, contents, and stated availability were checked on 28 October 2026. The EURAMET weighing and volume PDF endpoints timed out during automated inspection; their catalogue identities and download references were available. Preserve those limits when describing an inspected source. Freely readable NPL, EURAMET, Eurachem, and JCGM publications retain their respective rights; NIST federal text and third-party components can have different terms. The ISO standard is identified as a restricted professional reference rather than an open text.

